What Actually Changed

Let’s skip the marketing fluff. This is how all the Kotlin 2.3 multiplatform updates that matter:

1. Sensible Native Interop That Plays Nice With You

Swift/Objective-C interop previously felt like ancient language translations. Version 2.3 of Kotlin directly supports annotations to export more idiomatic APIs on iOS, generating cleaner APIs.

@ObjCName("UserRepository")
class UserDataRepository {
    @ObjCName("fetchUserProfile")
    suspend fun getUserProfile(userId: String): UserProfile {
        return api.fetchUser(userId)
    }
}

You get Swift code that looks like Swift instead of Java pretending to be Swift passing through the iOS team members.
